---Capture payment
---
---Captures the full amount of a card payment created with `capture: false`. The payment must still be in `requires_capture` before `capture_expires_at`. Partial capture, multiple captures, capturing more than the authorized amount, and tips are not supported.
---
---`POST /payments/{id}/capture`
---Errors: Forbidden, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input whop.payments.CapturePaymentRequest
---@return whop.payments.PaymentStatus? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:capture_payment(input) end

---Create Payment
---
---Charges a buyer for one or more plans. Pass a payment method already on file (`member_id` and `payment_method_id`), or a `confirmation_token` describing a method the buyer just supplied. Collection runs in the background: the response is the payment as created, not its outcome — poll Retrieve status for how far it has got and, for a confirmation-token payment, what the buyer must still do. Pass `line_items` for one or more plans with quantities, `plan_id` for an existing plan, or `plan` to find or create one inline. These inputs are mutually exclusive.
---
---`POST /payments`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input whop.payments.CreatePaymentRequest
---@return whop.payments.Payment? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_payment(input) end

---Retrieve Payment
---
---Returns one payment, including every purchased line item with its quantity and subtotal. Related records are ids — resolve a plan, membership, member or shipment on its own endpoint, and list this payment's refunds, disputes or Resolution Center cases with `?payment_id=`.
---
---`GET /payments/{id}`
---Errors: Forbidden, NotFound.
---@param input whop.payments.GetPaymentRequest
---@return whop.payments.Payment? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:get_payment(input) end

---Retrieve payment status
---
---Retrieves how far a payment has got and what the buyer must do next, if anything. A payment is collected in the background, so poll this rather than reading the create response. Accepts either a secret key or the payment's own `client_secret`, so the surface collecting the payment can poll it directly.
---
---`GET /payments/{payment_id}/status`
---Errors: Forbidden, NotFound.
---@param input whop.payments.GetStatusPaymentRequest
---@return whop.payments.PaymentStatus? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:get_status_payment(input) end

---List Payment Fees
---
---Returns the fee breakdown of one payment — Whop's fee, processing, affiliate and other lines — each in the currency it was collected in and converted to the payment's settlement currency. The list is complete in one page.
---
---`GET /payments/{id}/fees`
---Errors: NotFound.
---@param input whop.payments.ListPaymentFeesRequest
---@return whop.payments.ListPaymentFeesResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:list_payment_fees(input) end

---List Payments
---
---Lists payments, newest first. Without filters this is every payment the caller can read: a company credential's own account, or for a user every account they can read payments for. Filters narrow by account, buyer, product, plan, membership, status, billing reason, currency, and creation window. Filtering by `billing_reason=subscription_cycle` also matches renewals recorded as `subscription_update`. `settlement_time_at` is null on list rows — retrieve the payment for it.
---
---`GET /payments`
---Errors: BadRequest.
---@param input? whop.payments.ListPaymentsRequest
---@return whop.payments.ListPaymentsResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:list_payments(input) end

---List Payments
---
---Lists payments, newest first. Without filters this is every payment the caller can read: a company credential's own account, or for a user every account they can read payments for. Filters narrow by account, buyer, product, plan, membership, status, billing reason, currency, and creation window. Filtering by `billing_reason=subscription_cycle` also matches renewals recorded as `subscription_update`. `settlement_time_at` is null on list rows — retrieve the payment for it.
---
---Every page, fetched as the loop asks for it.
---
---`GET /payments`
---Errors: BadRequest.
---@param input? whop.payments.ListPaymentsRequest
---@return distilled.Iterator<whop.payments.ListPaymentsResponse>
function Client:list_payments_pages(input) end

---List Payments
---
---Lists payments, newest first. Without filters this is every payment the caller can read: a company credential's own account, or for a user every account they can read payments for. Filters narrow by account, buyer, product, plan, membership, status, billing reason, currency, and creation window. Filtering by `billing_reason=subscription_cycle` also matches renewals recorded as `subscription_update`. `settlement_time_at` is null on list rows — retrieve the payment for it.
---
---Every item of every page (`data`).
---
---`GET /payments`
---Errors: BadRequest.
---@param input? whop.payments.ListPaymentsRequest
---@return distilled.Iterator<whop.payments.Payment>
function Client:list_payments_items(input) end

---Refund Payment
---
---Issues a full or partial refund for a payment. The refund is processed through the original payment processor and the membership status is updated accordingly.
---
---`POST /payments/{id}/refund`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input whop.payments.RefundPaymentRequest
---@return whop.payments.Payment? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:refund_payment(input) end

---Resume a parked renewal
---
---Starts a fresh on-session attempt with the saved card for a subscription renewal that is waiting on the customer to authenticate; the bank's step then arrives in `next_action` on the following status reads. Only the payment's own customer may call it — with the payment's `client_secret` or their own session — and it is a no-op for any payment that is not a parked renewal.
---
---`POST /payments/{payment_id}/resume`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input whop.payments.ResumePaymentRequest
---@return whop.payments.PaymentStatus? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:resume_payment(input) end

---Retry Payment
---
---Retries a failed or pending payment. This re-attempts the charge using the original payment method and plan details.
---
---`POST /payments/{id}/retry`
---Errors: NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input whop.payments.RetryPaymentRequest
---@return whop.payments.Payment? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:retry_payment(input) end

---Update payment return URL
---
---Changes where the buyer lands after completing an off-site step, up until they return. Accepts either a secret key or the payment's own `client_secret`, so the surface that knows the final destination can set it.
---
---`PATCH /payments/{payment_id}/return_url`
---Errors: BadRequest.
---@param input whop.payments.UpdateReturnUrlPaymentRequest
---@return whop.payments.PaymentStatus? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:update_return_url_payment(input) end

---Void Payment
---
---Voids or cancels an eligible payment. The request is rejected if the payment is no longer eligible.
---
---`POST /payments/{id}/void`
---Errors: NotFound, Conflict.
---@param input whop.payments.VoidPaymentRequest
---@return whop.payments.Payment? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:void_payment(input) end

return Module
